<title>7 · The farm and the sieve — Sixty Years Later</title>
<meta name="description" content="Lem designed a machine that would grow scientific theories the way an egg grows an organism, and rejected Ashby's rival plan of generating everything and filtering it. The filter won. Sixty years on, the automation arrived where he pointed it — and the part he treated as solved, deciding what survives, is the part that is breaking.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../static/style.css">
<script src="../static/theme.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<header class="site-header">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="../index.html">Sixty Years <span>Later</span></a>
    <nav class="site-nav">
